WEBVTT

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.390
This can't be happening; I clasp my head in my hands

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:27.980
As I struggle with my desire to escape from this saturated world.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.400
Time goes flowing past with the rustling roar of sand.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.820
Things never get any better.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.740
I'm gazing on toward a dreamless tomorrow.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.040
I want to bid farewell to my days of constantly feeling lost.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.510
I try stretching out my hand in resistance.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:58.260
We'll cry millions upon millions of tears, then be reborn.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:04.390
Let's keep going, with red in our eyes, toward the future we drew for ourselves.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:10.150
Come over to me; I'm clapping my hands.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.110
Who are you? Where are you coming from?

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:16.450
I strain my eyes in the darkness.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:22.030
I can't see a thing, and nothing makes sense, but I'll go anyway.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:28.540
To the place where you're waiting, lit by a beacon of light.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.080
The detective still isn't back?

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.120
I wonder if something happened to him...

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.350
Sorry... You guys have a mystery or something?

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.120
Well, it's about the cucumbers at my farm;

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.140
they're almost ready to be picked!

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.140
Water is starting to leak through my walls again!

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:46.140
My cell phone is getting terrible service...

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.940
I want him to try out my food stand's new menu!

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.060
My precious necklace has disappeared somewhere! Please look for it!

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.060
How should I win back my girlfriend?!

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:51.900
Kazamori! Kazamori!

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.540
Well, considering the circumstances, Inga-chan will have to do!

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:55.770
Inga-chan, why not work for me part-time?

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.680
You won't have to do anything too indecent!

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.590
We'll just put you in a swimsuit!

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.590
Inga-chan is a boy!

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:00.610
That might be even better!

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.820
They're really starting to scare me...

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.190
You still haven't found Shinjuurou?!

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:06.260
Stop squeezing me!

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.200
Bamboo juice!

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.230
Where's Shinjuurou?

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:12.030
The firewalls are complex... Let me try again.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.050
Forget it, just help me out here!

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.740
Shinjuurou-sama!

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.630
Shinjuurou-sama!

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.560
Shinjuurou-sama!

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:26.660
Mamori... Kaze?

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.160
Kaza... Mori...

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.310
Was he there?

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.860
I found him. He's there, just as we thought.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.210
The Eastern Kantou Social Rehabilitation Promotion Center...

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:43.660
It may be privately run, but it's still a prison. Shinjuurou...

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.850
Shinjuurou said that he felt like he was being used when solving the case of the codes.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:51.390
He said he was going to the prison that guy is being kept in.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:54.220
If he was only visiting, it wouldn't take more than a couple of hours;

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:56.770
why on Earth has he been gone for days?

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:58.280
Can you fetch up any more details?

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:01.280
Our home connection is probably the most stable in all of Japan.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:06.030
Any average firewall could never stop me,

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:09.410
since part of me would have already combined with it in the cloud.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:15.120
Nonetheless, there's an aggressive barrier around Shinjuurou-sama that I'm unable to identify.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.790
You can't talk to Shinjuurou?

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:22.650
There are also some differences in his behaviour that I can't make sense of.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:25.930
I stole some footage from the surveillance cameras.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:35.810
It's an honour to be called upon by you, Chairman.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:38.190
Well, Rie was making quite a fuss.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.990
It seems that Yuuki Shinjuurou is indeed imprisoned in a privately run prison,

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:45.170
the Eastern Kantou Rehab Center.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:48.140
He has no criminal history, and hasn't been sentenced by any judges,

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.700
but he's been given a prisoner registration number.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:55.090
There's a possibility that someone has falsified the data.

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.710
What should we do about him?

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:00.350
Well, we may as well get him out of there for now.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:01.890
If he's innocent, that is.

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:03.960
Rie-sama! Please stop this at once!

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:08.840
I'm going too!

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:10.470
Milady...

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:14.230
Please let me go as your assistant, Izumi-san!

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:17.060
Assistants and maids are two different things...

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.020
Huh?!

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:28.320
Wait a minute!

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.200
I made these.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:35.970
I'll take 'em.

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:38.420
I'll put them to use if the detective starts acting up.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:47.390
So you were the one who remotely
attempted to make Yajima-shi kill his wife.

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:49.470
You refer to yourself as a novelist, but your real name is...

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:52.810
New characters have shown up in the middle of the story and messed up the plot...

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:55.190
Try not to talk too much.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.730
What did you do to the detective?

00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:58.440
Who are those women?

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.620
A murder occurred on site while filming a movie.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:02.440
Filming?

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:06.050
The culprit is the cameraman, Yuuki Shinjuurou.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.570
You're a high-class detective, got it?

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:20.180
Quit lagging behind!

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:21.420
Y-Yes, milady!

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:37.140
A murder?!

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:40.860
And you're saying that Prosecutor Koyama has arrested the culprit?

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.400
Everything seems a bit mixed up...

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.660
They're going to begin a more thorough investigation soon,

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.900
so it will probably take a while.

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:50.580
The prosecutor just happened to be here,

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:53.060
and with Kaishou Rie, a civilian;

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:55.030
there's no way they'd be able to carry out an investigation...

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:57.540
It's as if they're all seeing the same illusion-

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:01.500
An illusion... That's it!

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:06.430
This is similar to the Oono Myoushin case,

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:09.920
in which the founder of a new religious cult murdered his followers.

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:13.640
The followers were hallucinating to the
point of believing his words were reality.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.030
It was as if they were looking at a blank screen,

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:18.520
and seeing whatever Oono told them was there.

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:22.650
Oono had the power to make his words into reality.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:25.160
That's the power of Bettenou.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:28.530
Bettenou? The same Bettenou that was the founder of Oono's cult?

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:30.850
Bettenou is a god...

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:33.590
...one that turns people's words into reality.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:37.910
That's why I've been telling you that I can smell her here!

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:41.470
All you were saying was that something smelled strange!

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:42.580
But if that's the case...

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.830
Perhaps all this...

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.090
...is being caused by one of...

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:47.590
...Bettenou's illusions.

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:50.570
She must be using Shinjuurou and everyone in there to create some kind of story.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:51.760
It's probably about time I...

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:52.880
Click!

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:56.430
Maybe a little more...

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:00.930
Kazamori!

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:00.930
Bonus round!

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.260
So this... Is the mystery.

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:52.190
Yuuki-san?

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:01.260
Kazamori... The bonus round wasn't necessary.

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:02.830
It's nice to see you again.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:05.310
What can you see right now?

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.250
The truth, most likely.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.380
Sinners, huh?

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:15.720
Yes, the Metro Police informed me of it already...

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:20.100
If it's made public that someone who came here for a visit ended up as a prisoner...

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:24.210
For now, we have no choice but to leave it to them.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:27.190
Solving this murder takes priority!

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:25.600
I found the crime scene.

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:30.480
Do shutters without safety mechanisms even exist anymore?!

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:42.330
It's been modified to leave no record of it opening or closing!

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:45.080
The safety mechanisms are disabled as well...

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.790
Non-existent streetcars don't run.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:09:58.880
This is the murder weapon.

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:02.420
This shutter is only used to separate the mens and womens quarters,

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:04.980
so it's rarely even used.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:08.400
Director Mitaka... I mean, the security guard, I guess...

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:12.190
He was opening this shutter nightly in order to visit the women's block...

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.810
...in order to make contact with a female prisoner.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:18.200
That's why the circuit was cut.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.150
Cut it out already!

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:24.180
Why is our prime suspect acting the
detective and conducting an investigation?

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.030
It's just as Milady says.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:27.580
Milady is the pride of our department.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.080
She solves cases with money, authority, and sheer will;

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:32.320
she's known to all as "The High-class Detective"!

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:36.090
I guess that novelist can't write light novels...

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:39.230
I'm going to go confirm the identity of this "novelist".

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.220
Don't forget about Bettenou.

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:43.760
I'm through with being obstructed by her.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:46.380
Huh? You think you're coming along?

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:48.230
As if they'd let a kid in...

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.630
They wouldn't have a problem with me, would they?

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:54.480
I can go as your assistant.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:56.980
O-Of course!

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:58.860
Leave the handcuffs on.

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:03.820
If you don't keep applying stimulus, you'll be sucked back into that novelist's tale.

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:06.240
Oh, and if it looks like they're going to cause you trouble...

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:07.800
Yuuki Shinjuurou!

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:08.250
Ah, like this?

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:10.640
How long do you plan to keep up this farce?!

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:15.850
W-What are you doing?!

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:20.660
If you resist me, I'll sentence you to 780 years of imprisonment!

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.660
"Ah, I'm so scared!"

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:21.550
In parentheses, with a monotone voice.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:29.680
All of the prisoners here are monitored
using their individually numbered chips.

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:32.560
This is the recording of the area around the shutter from last night.

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:36.230
That's me.

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:42.310
There were no other numbers, and therefore prisoners, in the area until the morning.

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:46.610
In other words, no one could have been the culprit but you, Defeated Detective!

00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:48.240
Why would I...?

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.710
I can imagine it happening.

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:50.930
You probably screamed,

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:53.060
"The truth must be revealed", like you always do,

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:54.630
and got in a fight with the guy.

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:57.960
After all, you've got a terrible mouth, but a stronger sense of justice than anyone.

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:00.410
Is that praise? Or an insult?

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:03.510
Those numbers...

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:05.140
Did you notice something?

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:09.580
I was placed in here by a man claiming to be a novelist.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:14.140
But is it possible to issue a new number to me when I'm not a criminal?

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:19.400
There's a lot of maintenance that's necessary with
mounting the chips, so even a guard can install them.

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:23.400
But the registered numbers are issued by the courts and public prosecutors.

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:29.050
In that case, an existing prisoner's number may have been transferred to my chip.

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:30.790
That is a possibility...

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:33.700
Then, if there's another prisoner with that same number...

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:37.290
Our security system wouldn't allow a
double registration of the same number!

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:40.060
That just means that, even if they have a chip attached,

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:44.930
we have one prisoner here who doesn't have a registered number.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:49.050
That prisoner can move about without the security system monitoring them.

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:50.890
There are surveillance cameras though!

00:12:50.890 --> 00:12:52.650
The victim was probably tampering with the angles of the cameras,

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:55.640
just as he was able to modify the shutter,

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:58.370
so that no one could detect his movements.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.910
I'll start checking immediately!

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:02.110
If we can find who originally had your number,

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:03.680
we'll have the killer!

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:05.070
No.

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:10.230
There wasn't ever a war.

00:13:10.230 --> 00:13:14.240
If I solve this mystery, the dream that novelist gave us will disappear.

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:21.630
Bring me the criminal records of your female prisoners!

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:24.760
I wonder what will happen to the movie...

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:27.330
I don't want it to get cancelled...

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.890
...just when I felt I'd finally been able to accomplish something.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.140
We don't even know the conclusion yet...

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.270
Shinjuurou-kun!

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:46.950
Before his murder, Director Mitaka
was looking for movies in the library.

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:52.800
Stuart Rosenberg, Franklin J. Shaffner, Frank Darabont.

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.720
Can you tell me what all of them have in common?

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:56.860
They're all foreigners!

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:00.460
They each directed a famous prison break movie.

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:01.880
Prison break?

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.500
When I saw the director...

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:07.630
You get it, don't you?! You're a papillon!

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:09.690
No! You mustn't let go!

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:10.760
Please don't let go!

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:11.610
I'm begging you!

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:13.490
He called the woman a "papillon"...

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:13.160
Let go of me!

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.770
Please, just listen to me!

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.770
...and begged her to not let go of him?

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:18.130
Was that the final line of a breakup?

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:22.050
No. He wasn't telling her not to let go.

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.160
"Please, don't tell anyone."

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.160
TL Note: The words for "speaking" and "letting go" have the same pronunciation.

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:29.090
He was telling the woman, who knew his secret, not to tell anyone.

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:31.950
The director had a secret and that's why he was killed?

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:33.330
Isn't that a bit backwards?

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:36.750
The reason the director was entering the women's block nightly...

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:40.040
...was to help the woman who knew his secret escape this prison.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:44.080
He was trying to find even the smallest hint by looking into those movies.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:46.200
Escape this prison?

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:49.810
If he switched out her prisoner number and altered the cameras, it would be possible.

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:53.180
I don't understand... What prison are you talking about?

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:57.160
I solved the mystery.

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.890
These are your finishing lines.

00:15:02.490 --> 00:15:07.490
"Yes... I was really just a simple NEET, pretending to be a hacker."

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:09.020
What is this?

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:16.250
"It was so much fun leaking the
governments confidential information,"

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:21.080
"but once my blog started getting attention, I even began uploading lies."

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:23.790
"One day, the police came..."

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:30.110
"I had relations with more people than I could count..."

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:32.630
"...because I was so insecure."

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:37.780
"Is this war going to last forever? I fear it may never end..."

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:41.730
"I wanted to be with someone so that I could forget my anxiety,"

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:47.900
"but when the war ended, I was accused of selling my body."

00:15:57.110 --> 00:16:00.040
I was merely an ordinary mother.

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:03.030
I couldn't allow my son, who wasn't even a year old,

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:05.920
to become a victim of the war.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:09.800
I simply wanted to protect my everyday life.

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:12.790
That's why I accepted a friend's invitation,

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:14.680
and participated in a demonstration against the government.

00:16:15.090 --> 00:16:16.170
Before long, I thought,

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:19.430
"If that prime minister doesn't quit, the war will never end."

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:22.930
"And... If he won't quit, I'll just make him quit."

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:25.740
I researched how to make explosives...

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:28.940
...then one day, the Public Security Force came.

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:34.450
During the war, there were many bombing plots against the Prime Minister that were uncovered,

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:38.040
but among them was a housewife who was trying to protect her everyday life?

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:42.140
Mitaka Kichitarou also participated in demonstrations against the government during the war...

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:44.140
...and met Izawa Sayo there.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:48.830
But to him, those demonstrations were nothing more than a fad of the times.

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:52.470
Now that he was working as a security guard for a private prison following the war,

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:58.120
he would lose his job and his future if it was known he'd interacted with terrorists.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:03.090
So that's why he switched out Izawa Sayo's number and tried to help her escape?

00:17:05.840 --> 00:17:08.940
Mitaka asked me something once.

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:11.020
Tanimura and Yada are over there, right?

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:12.730
Izawa, too?

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:16.610
At that time, you were behind the shadow of that box, and he couldn't see you.

00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:22.250
But Mitaka's tablet displays each prisoner's number and location in real time,

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:26.000
so even if he couldn't see you, there
shouldn't have been a need to ask me.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:27.870
So then, why did he ask?

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:31.960
Izawa Sayo...

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:35.470
...it's because your number is the only one that isn't displayed.

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:44.860
He told me, "I'll get you out of here, so don't tell anyone!"

00:17:44.860 --> 00:17:46.480
But I didn't understand.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:49.650
I'm shooting a movie.

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:53.460
I thought that I would be able to finish...

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:56.240
...and become my true self!

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:58.780
Why should I have to be cut from the movie?!

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:00.950
That's why I...

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.250
He was trying to help you escape!

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:10.490
He probably pitied that you couldn't be with your child...

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:11.170
No!

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:12.290
It was the streetcar!

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:14.710
It moved! It moved,

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:16.010
and ran him over!

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:18.250
Is not war but a toy?

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:19.680
I'm not the only one who think this.

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:24.140
You... You too, have been treating war as a toy.

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:52.030
Are you that frustrated that, this one time, the great Yuuki Shinjuurou...

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:56.420
...had to rely on Chairman Kaishou's deductions?

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:58.380
You're making a terrible face.

00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:02.430
You know, I'm going to stick around here a bit longer.

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:05.930
I want to escape, but I can't run from this opportunity;

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:12.060
this is a chance to reflect upon myself from a more thorough perspective.

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:29.790
Wandering hazily on a pale morning, hearing a whispered prayer,

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:37.750
You and I trace a twisted scenery.

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:45.430
We're seeking the (truth). "We don't even care if it's a lie."

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:49.810
As if we can see right through it,

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:53.770
We follow it along.

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:57.730
Looking for, going beyond words,

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:01.740
Like a falling feather.

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:04.860
Looking for, find it,

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:11.200
So we can come closer together.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:29.720
Looking for, unravel it,

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:33.730
Tear it apart, like a cloud.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:36.810
Looking for, find it,

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:41.650
So we can come closer together.

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:54.330
Something's wrong...

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:58.570
Answer me. What is it you want?

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:01.090
What are you trying to do with Yuuki Shinjuurou?

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:03.930
You won't be able to resist.

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:07.880
Humans have no choice but to answer my question.

00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:12.400
And until you've done so, you won't even be able to call that mischievous god of yours.

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:21.480
What are you trying to do with Yuuki Shinjuurou?

00:21:21.990 --> 00:21:25.330
He's my... Great Detective.

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:26.240
Ooh!

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:28.840
I'm a novelist.

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:32.000
Using this reality as a stage, I bring forth events.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:34.140
That is my novel...

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:37.590
...and every novel needs a detective.

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:39.400
I wanted to keep him near me,

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:42.650
so that I could continue writing new works.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.630
I have an innumerable amount of plots!

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:48.270
And that's why you forced the security guard to help you,

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:51.450
and disguised Shinjuurou as a prisoner.

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:54.760
Then I disposed of that security guard;

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:56.890
it was the detective's first case!

00:21:57.400 --> 00:22:00.930
But he mustn't solve the mystery!

00:22:00.930 --> 00:22:05.650
Because if he did, the wonderful world of illusion would begin to break down!

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:11.160
He was supposed to eternally grapple with an unsolvable mystery in an illusionary world.

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:13.880
He was supposed to become mine!

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:21.540
That's too bad. There's no such thing as a mystery Yuuki Shinjuurou can't solve.

00:22:21.540 --> 00:22:25.170
Even if he has to spill every drop of his blood in the process...

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:30.300
He always offers me more truths... more souls...

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:43.770
Where's Bettenou?

00:22:44.350 --> 00:22:47.040
You didn't take her away yourself?

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:48.530
The way you always do...

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:55.870
"If someone hadn't killed him, I might have killed him myself."

00:22:56.230 --> 00:22:58.820
"Instead of going to all this trouble to look for the criminal,

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:02.080
I'd rather hunt down the killer of Takeda Shingen,

00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:07.630
who might've died of natural causes, suicide, <i>or</i> murder,"

00:23:07.630 --> 00:23:11.250
Shinjurou answered with a scowl.

00:23:11.250 --> 00:23:13.930
Inspired by "The Sneering Demon" from Ango Torimonochou,

00:23:13.930 --> 00:23:16.930
Next time on UN-GO: "Kaishou Rinroku's Crime".

00:23:16.930 --> 00:23:18.770
There's a reason I'm so sherious...

00:23:18.770 --> 00:23:21.100
I mean serious! I'm serious!
